IX. Coordination in Review of Draft ORV Environmental Statement
In response to requests for review of the draft ORV environmental statement, comments were received from seven Federal agencies in addition to those received from the seven bureaus within the Department of the Interior. These comments have been incorporated, as applicable, into the final environmental statement and the Departmental ORV regulations. In summary these comments were as follows:
1) Department of Commerce, Deputy Assistant Secretary for Environmental Affairs  suggested that environmental statement, on page 12, lines 3 and 4, delineate those resources affected and to what degree by the proposed action; called our attention to 16 USC 478 which provides for access to public lands for purpose of prospecting;
2) Department of Defense, Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense (Environmental Quality) - indicated that environmental statement is satisfactory;
3) Department of Health, Education, and Welfare,
Assistant Secretary for Health and Scientific Affairs felt that human impacts portion of environmental
statement gave inadequate attention to potential public
health hazards associated with use of ORV;
4) Department of Transportation, Assistant Secretary for Environment and Urban Systems  indicated concern over noise emitted by ORV. Suggested that environmental statement include a statement on the need to develop appropriate noise standards;
Activities  indicated particular interest in adverse noise impacts of ORV and the measures to be taken to protect the public from noise levels. With regard to noise standards and criteria, advised that EPA will be promulgating standards and regulations for recreational vehicles under Section 6 of the Noise Control Act of 1972, and that these standards will apply to the manufacture of such vehicles, but will be based, among other things, on the conditions of use of the vehicle. Further indicated that EPA believes these standards will be of assistance to land managers in applying noise-level criteria for ORV use on Interior lands;
